{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% import 'macros.html.twig' as ui %}

{% block title %}RMF Rev 5 Controls{% endblock %}
{% block og_title %}NIST 800-53 Rev 5 — security and privacy controls{% endblock %}
{% block og_description %}NIST 800-53 r5 — every control with baseline-membership badges (NIST L/M/H/Privacy, FedRAMP, CNSSI 1253), linked CCIs, and STIG cross-references.{% endblock %}
{% block og_image_name %}rmf{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <article class="stig-detail">
        <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
            <ol>
                <li><a href="{{ path('home') }}">Library</a></li>
                <li aria-current="page">800-53 r5</li>
            </ol>
        </nav>

        <header class="stig-detail__header">
            <div class="stig-detail__header-text">
                <span class="eyebrow">NIST SP 800-53</span>
                <h1 class="stig-detail__title">
                    Risk Management Framework <em>Rev. 5</em>
                </h1>
                <div class="stig-detail__meta">
                    <span>{{ rmf.xpath("/controls:controls/controls:control")|length|number_format }} controls</span>
                    <span>&middot; Current revision</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="stig-detail__actions">
                <button type="button" class="icon-btn" onclick="pdf_app.exec();" title="Print" aria-label="Print">
                    <i class="bi bi-printer-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
            </div>
        </header>

        <div class="doc-desc">
            <p>Information security controls protect the confidentiality, integrity and/or availability of information (the so-called CIA Triad). Again, some would add further categories such as non-repudiation and accountability, depending on how narrowly or broadly the CIA Triad is defined.</p>
            <p>Individual controls are often designed to act together to increase effective protection. Systems of controls can be referred to as frameworks or standards. Frameworks can enable an organization to manage security controls across different types of assets with consistency. For example, a framework can help an organization manage controls over access regardless of the type of computer operating system. This also enables an organization to assess overall risk. Risk-aware organizations may choose proactively to specify, design, implement, operate and maintain their security controls, usually by assessing the risks and implementing a comprehensive security management framework such as ISO27001:2013, the Information Security Forum&rsquo;s Standard of Good Practice for Information Security, or NIST SP 800-53.</p>
        </div>

        {% set total_controls = rmf.xpath("/controls:controls/controls:control")|length %}
        <div class="lib-page__bar rmf-filter-bar">
            <div class="lib-page__filter">
                <span class="lib-page__filter-label eyebrow">Baseline</span>
                <div class="chip-group" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Filter controls by baseline">
                    <button type="button" class="chip active" data-overlay="all"
                            onclick="window.app.rmfList.filter(this)">
                        All <span class="chip-count">{{ total_controls|number_format }}</span>
                    </button>
                    {% for o in overlays %}
                        {% set enh = o.count - o.row_count %}
                        <button type="button" class="chip chip--{{ o.level }}" data-overlay="{{ o.id }}"
                                onclick="window.app.rmfList.filter(this)"
                                title="{{ o.title }} — {{ o.row_count|number_format }} rows visible{% if enh > 0 %} ({{ o.count|number_format }} controls total incl. {{ enh|number_format }} enhancement{{ enh == 1 ? '' : 's' }} nested in parent rows){% endif %}">
                            {{ o.short_title }} <span class="chip-count">{{ o.row_count|number_format }}</span>
                        </button>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            </div>
            <div id="rmf-page-info" class="rmf-filter-bar__info"
                 data-total="{{ total_controls }}" aria-live="polite">
                Showing {{ total_controls|number_format }} controls
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rule-text">&sect; Controls</div>

    {% for control in rmf.xpath("/controls:controls/controls:control") %}
        {% set ctrl_num = control.number|trim %}
        {% set ctrl_overlays = overlay_map[ctrl_num]|default([]) %}
        <section class="control-card"
                 data-control="{{ ctrl_num }}"
                 data-overlays="{{ ctrl_overlays|join(' ') }}">
        <a id="rmf_{{control.number}}"></a>
        {% set res = control.registerXPathNamespace("aaa", "http://scap.nist.gov/schema/sp800-53/2.0") %}
        {% set res = control.registerXPathNamespace("controls", "http://scap.nist.gov/schema/sp800-53/feed/2.0") %}
        {% set res = rmf.registerXPathNamespace("aaa", "http://scap.nist.gov/schema/sp800-53/2.0") %}
        {% set res = rmf.registerXPathNamespace("controls", "http://scap.nist.gov/schema/sp800-53/feed/2.0") %}
        <div class="req-header">
            {{control.title}}
        </div>

        <div class="container-fluid">
            <div class="row">
                <dl class="col-12 col-md-2 mb-0 p-0 pl-1 g-0 border border-1 bg-light">
                    <dt class="">RMF Control</dt>
                    <dd class="">{{ ui.ident(control.number) }}</dd>

                    <dt class="">Subject Area</dt>
                    <dd class="">{{control.family}}</dd>

                    <dt class="">Baselines</dt>
                    <dd class="baseline-badges">
                        {% if ctrl_overlays|length %}
                            {% for oid in ctrl_overlays %}
                                {% set o = overlays[oid] %}
                                <span class="baseline-badge baseline-badge--{{ o.level }}"
                                      title="{{ o.title }}">{{ o.abbr }}</span>
                            {% endfor %}
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="baseline-badge baseline-badge--none"
                                  title="Not in any current NIST or FedRAMP baseline">&mdash;</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </dd>

                </dl>
                <div class="col-12 col-md-7 pt-0 mt-0">
<div class="sec-header">Description</div>
<div class="req-desc pre-wrap">{% for i in control.xpath('./aaa:discussion/aaa:description/aaa:p') %}{{ i.asXml()|striptags|trans}}
{% endfor %}</div>
<div class="sec-header">Instructions</div>
{{control.xpath('./aaa:statement/aaa:description')|join(', ')}}
<dl>{% for i in control.xpath('./aaa:statement/aaa:statement') %}
    <dt class="inline">{{ i.number }}</dt>
    <dd>{{ i.description }}</dd>
{% endfor %}
</dl>

<div class="sec-header">Assessment Procedures</div>
<div class="container">
<dl>
{% for r in rmfs_json%}
{% if r.id == control.number %}
{% for ap in r.ccis %}
<dt >{{ ui.ident(ap.ap_acronym) }} - {{ ui.cci_link(ap.id) }}</dt>
<dd class="text-sm">{{ ap.definition }}</dd>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</dl>
</div>

<div class="sec-header">Related Controls</div>
<div class="container">
<ol class="row">  
{% for r in control.xpath('./aaa:related') %}
    <li class="col-3  reference">
        <a href="#rmf_{{r}}">
            {{ ui.ident(r) }}
        </a>
        -
        {% set related_control = rmf.xpath("/controls:controls/controls:control[aaa:number='" ~ r ~ "']")|first %}
        {% if related_control %}
            {{ related_control.title|title }}
        {% endif %}
    </li>

{% endfor %}
</ol>
</div>


<div class="sec-header">References</div>
<div class="container">
<ol class="row">  
{% for r in control.xpath('./aaa:references/aaa:reference') %}
    <li class="col-4  reference">
        {{r.item.text}},
        "{{r.short_name}}"
        <a href="{{r.item.attributes.href}}">
            {{"%.50s"|format(r.item.attributes.href)}}
        </a>
        
    </li>
{% endfor %}
</ol>
</div>

                </div>

                <div class="col-12 col-md-3 mb-0 p-0 pl-1 g-0 border border-1 bg-light">
<div class="sec-header">Enhancements</div>                        
<dl class="text-sm">
{% for r in control.xpath('./aaa:control-enhancements/aaa:control-enhancement') %}
    <dt class="">
        {{ ui.ident(r.number) }} - {{ r.title|title }}

    </dt>
    <dd>{{r.statement.description}}</dd>
{% endfor %}
</dl>
                </div>    


            </div>
        </div>
        </section>

        {% set break = true %}
    {% endfor %}
    </article>
    <script>
        const rmf_app = {
            init(){
                     
            },
        };

        pdf_app = {
	toTitleCase(str){
	  return str.replace(
		/\w\S*/g,
		text => text.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + text.substring(1).toLowerCase()
	  );
	},
	exec(){
		let printWindow = window.open('', '', 'height=1024,width=1280');
		printWindow.document.write('<html><head><title>RMFv5 Controls</title>');
		printWindow.document.write('<style>body{font-family:arial;}</style>');
		printWindow.document.write('</head><body >');
		
		$('.req-header').each( (i, e)=>{
			printWindow.document.write("<h1>" + $(e).next('div').find('div.row > dl > dd')[0].innerText + " - " + e.innerText + "</h1>");
			printWindow.document.write("<p>" + pdf_app.toTitleCase($(e).next('div').find('div.row > dl > dd')[1].innerText) + " - " + pdf_app.toTitleCase($(e).next('div').find('div.row > dl > dd')[2].innerText) + "</p>")
			
			printWindow.document.write("<h2>Description:</h2>")
			printWindow.document.write("<p>" + $(e).next('div').find('div.row > div.col-7 > div.req-desc').html() + "</p>")
		
			printWindow.document.write("<blockquote>")
				printWindow.document.write("<h2>Instructions:</h2>")
				$(e).next('div').find('div.row > div.col-7 > dl').each( (ii, ee)=>{
					printWindow.document.write($(ee).html())
				})
				
				printWindow.document.write("<h2>Assessment Procedures:</h2>")
				$(e).next('div').find('div.row > div.col-7 > div.container > dl').each( (ii, ee)=>{
					printWindow.document.write($(ee).html())
				})
				
				printWindow.document.write("<h2>Related Controls:</h2>")
				$(e).next('div').find('div.row > div > div.container > ol > li.col-3.reference').each( (ii, ee)=>{
					printWindow.document.write("<li>" + $(ee).text().trim().replaceAll("\n","").replace(/\s+/g, ' ') + "</li>")
				})
				
				printWindow.document.write("<h2>Enhancements:</h2>")
				$(e).next('div').find('div.row > div.col-3 > dl').each( (ii, ee)=>{
					printWindow.document.write($(ee).html())
				})
				
				printWindow.document.write("<h2>References:</h2>")
				$(e).next('div').find('div.row > div > div.container > ol > li.col-4.reference').each( (ii, ee)=>{
					printWindow.document.write("<li style='font-size:8pt;'>" + $(ee).html() + "</li>" )
				})
			
			printWindow.document.write("</blockquote>")
			printWindow.document.write("<hr />"  )			
		})
		printWindow.document.write('</body></html>');
		printWindow.document.close();
	}
};

        $(document).ready( () => {
            rmf_app.init();
        })
    </script>
{% endblock %}